 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the Long Island Gay, Lesbian, Bisexual and Transgender Health and Human Services Network, Inc., to file an application for retroactive tax exempt status",
    "basePrintNo": "S7809",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7809-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7809\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the Long Island Gay, Lesbian,\nBisexual and Transgender Health and Human Services Network, Inc., to\nfile an application for retroactive tax exempt status\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo grant the town assessor for the town of Brookhaven the authority to\nexempt the Long Island Gay, Lesbian, Bisexual and Transgender Health\nand Human Services Network, Inc. from liability for payment of real\nproperty taxes due on the 2013-2014 assessment roll.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One authorizes the assessor of the town of Brookhaven to\naccept an application from the Long Island Gay, Lesbian, Bisexual and\nTransgender Health and Human Services Network, Inc., for exemption\nfrom real property taxes pursuant to Section 462 of the real property\nlaw for the assessment roll as completed in 2013-2014. Upon\nsatisfaction that the organization, would have otherwise been entitled\nto exemption, had the property been used by an officiating clergyman\nfor residential purposes, and had said application been filed in a\ntimely manner, the assessor may grant this exemption from all taxation\nwith respect to the 2013-2014 roll. If the exemption is granted, the\norganization may be refunded any taxes paid and cancel any taxes,\nfines, penalties and interest remaining unpaid.\n\nSection Two is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Long Island Gay, Lesbian, Bisexual and Transgender Health and\nHuman Services Network, Inc., is a not for profit, occupying a\nbuilding located at 7 Crossway Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772. The\norganization purchased this property on April 8, 2014, missing the\ntaxable status by which an application for exemption from real\nproperties must be filed. This legislation would allow the\norganization the ability to file a late application for forgiveness\nfrom property taxes due on the 2013-2014 roll.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
